CHANGELOG.md

# src/icons is excluded because it cannot be formatted.
#
# Every icon is `factory("Name", <shapes/>)` with the shapes as bare siblings, so a composite icon is
# not parseable JSX — `JSX expressions must have one parent element` — and prettier's behaviour on a
# file it cannot parse is to leave it alone rather than fail loudly. Running `prettier --write` over
# the directory therefore produced a confusing half-applied result: files that had been repaired were
# rewritten back to their unparseable form while the errors went unreported, because `lint` and
# `typecheck` were not part of that command.
#
# The icons are wrapped in a `<g>` now, which parses. They stay out of prettier's path regardless, so
# that a future formatting run cannot silently undo it — a formatter that rewrites files it cannot
# read is worse than one that skips them.
